1.Problem Statement 
  Develop a C++ program to represent hospital equipment units as vertices and possible wiring links as weighted edges.
  Apply Kruskal's algorithm to select the minimum-cost wiring connections. Display selected edges and total wiring cost, 
  and list edges rejected because they create cycles.

2.Soiution
  The hospital equipment wiring problem is solved using Kruskal’s Algorithm. Each hospital equipment unit is represented as a vertex,
  and each possible wiring connection is represented as a weighted edge.
  First, all edges are sorted in ascending order of their costs. The algorithm selects the lowest-cost edge that does not create a cycle.
  The Disjoint Set Union (DSU) data structure is used to detect cycles. The process continues until all equipment units are connected or
  all edges have been checked.
  Finally, the program displays the selected wiring connections, the minimum total wiring cost, and the rejected edges that create cycles.
  This approach helps connect hospital equipment with minimum cost while avoiding unnecessary wiring connections.
